Dock z-index 11, scrim 19, panels 21. On mobile, dock z-index still 11 but scrim 19 would cover dock, so clicking the sheet buttons after one sheet open? When a sheet is open, scrim covers dock; that's intended (can't click dock while sheet open), but the close buttons are in panel (21). Fine.

Crucially, when opening the sheet, the scrim becomes visible with z-index 19 above dock z-index 11. The **pointerdown** lands on the button (scrim was invisible initially). Then pointerup may land on scrim (now covering button) -> click event target may be scrim? Actually the click target is computed as the nearest common ancestor of pointerdown and pointerup targets. If pointerdown target = button (in dock), pointerup target = scrim, the click is dispatched to their common ancestor (#app or body), not the button. Then why did sheet open at all? Because perhaps `pointerdown` and `pointerup` target still button's? Hmm, when element moves? In our click with force, the mouse down/up maybe both process synchronously before CSS applies? The scrim is added in JS click event (which fires after pointerup), so it can't affect the same click. Right: click fires after up, so the scrim becomes visible after the click is dispatched. No click-through. So not that.

But there are **two** listeners on the button? Look at the bindings: `#btn-sheet-specimen` listener only once. Also maybe a keyboard-driven click? no.

At dev 768, class after click was not sheet-open. That means openSheet ran then closeSheets? Only possibility is another listener on same button calling close: none. Or class was never added because `openSheet` not called. But then after 1.5s transform 481 implies it was moving. Wait if class never added, transform should be closed 690 immediately, not 481. Unless the panel's transition is just *starting* from 0 to 690 because the mobile media query just applied (after viewport change) and the panel is transitioning from initial desktop position? At page.goto after setViewport, on load the class maybe still has sheet-open from previous page? No reload resets DOM. `#specimen-panel` no sheet-open. The media query applies at load; transform starts? The element begins with desktop position (no transform -> transform none = 0), then media query sets translateY(690) which triggers a transition from 0 to 690 on initial style application! Ah yes: because the element has `transition: transform 320ms` in mobile mode, and the browser applies the media rule, it animates from default 0 to 690 at load. So `transform 481` at 1.5s is just the **closing animation on page load**, still not finished due to slow compositor. And the sheet class never got applied because... the button click? Hmm.

If the sheet class were applied, class would show. It didn't. At 768 dev, after clicking 1.8s after load, class stayed "panel specimen-panel". That means the click did not trigger the handler. Why? Maybe because the dock button was **covered by the invisible/scrim?** Scrim visibility hidden at load, not covering. Or by the **closed sheet**? The specimen sheet itself is transformed down to y=842..? top 360 initially? Hmm at 768, closed sheet top maybe ~? It could overlap the dock due to slow transition. The sheet is at z-index 21, above dock. While it's animating closed from 0 to 690, it may cover the dock and intercept the click. Since compositor slow, at click time (1.8s), the sheet might still be over the dock (transform 481, top 842? Wait top 842 is below the dock y=965? Actually 842 < 965, so sheet starts above dock and extends down beyond viewport, covering the dock area! Yes! Closed sheet should be translated fully below, with top ~? The panel height maybe 546, bottom 84, transform 690 => top = 1024-84-? Let's calculate: bottom = 84 -> untransformed top = 1024 - 84 - height. If height=546, top=394. +690 = 1084. But measured top 1050 with transform 690 => base top=360, height? bottom=84 => height=580. yes top=1084? 360+690=1050? bottom then 1050+580=1630. Base bottom 940 = 1024-84. Good. So when transform 690, top=1050 (below viewport), no overlap. But during load transition from 0 to 690, at transform 481, top=841, and it extends to 1421, covering dock at 965. Since it is z-index 21, it intercepts clicks on the dock! That explains why the click did nothing at dev 768: the sheet was still sliding closed and covering the dock. At production, maybe by click time it had reached 690 (class absent? no, class became sheet-open there after click; so click did register). Production: click registered, sheet opened (class sheet-open), but transform stayed 690 because it started from 690 and transitions to 0—should animate. But maybe it's also stuck due to slow compositor, and we only waited 1.5s. So both are timing issues in the software renderer, not functional bugs on real hardware.

But there IS a real UX bug: on initial load, mobile panels animate from 0 to closed 690, briefly covering the scene/dock for the first ~320ms (or longer in slow rendering). Because the transition applies the closed transform after load. On real hardware, 320ms flash of panels sliding down at page load. Did we see that in mobile screenshot? After 2.2s, closed. But could be a flash. Ideally, avoid transition on initial state. Add a class to enable transitions only after first frame / when opening. Or use `visibility` to prevent closed panels intercepting clicks, and disable transition on load.

Also closed panels remain in DOM translated below viewport but still potentially intercept? They're below, so no. But during initial transition they cover. More robust: add `visibility: hidden` when closed, `visibility: visible` when sheet-open. Visibility isn't animatable but can be transitioned with delay; then closed panels never intercept. And avoid initial slide by adding a `.sheets-ready` class after load.

Simplest robust fix:
- In mobile media, set `visibility: hidden;` on `.specimen-panel,.ecology-panel` and `pointer-events: none;` with transition include visibility 0s linear 320ms.
- `.sheet-open` gets `visibility: visible; pointer-events: auto; transition-delay: 0s` (and transform). That prevents interception while closed and during load.
- The initial slide-down flash still could show but visibility hidden from the start means it's not visible. Good.

But `.sheet-open` transition visibility should switch immediately: `transition: transform 320ms ..., visibility 0s linear 320ms;` closed. For open: `transition: transform 320ms ..., visibility 0s;` so visible immediately. Or use `visibility: visible` with no transition. CSS:
```
.specimen-panel, .ecology-panel {
  visibility: hidden;
  pointer-events: none;
  transition: transform 320ms ..., visibility 0s linear 320ms;
}
.specimen-panel.sheet-open,... {
  visibility: visible;
  pointer-events: auto;
  transform: translateY(0);
  transition: transform 320ms ..., visibility 0s;
}
```
This also means during closing, visibility stays visible for 320ms then hidden, preserving animation. Good. But with slow compositor, pointer-events none applies immediately on close (not delayed), okay.

Also initial state no transition from 0? visibility hidden, so no flash. The transform still animates from 0 but invisible, doesn't matter. It won't intercept because pointer-events none.

This is a genuine improvement. Let's implement. Also note the sheet close button click while open works.

Then retest 768: even if sheet still covering due to opening animation, dock is underneath scrim anyway once open; but initial click will register since panel hidden.

